---
description: Reconcile grant-specific service periods, restrictions, spending, activity claims and submission lifecycle.
args: { request: GrantCycleRequest; ledger: GrantEvidenceLedger }
returns: GrantProgramResult
uses: [grantDesk/deriveAwardConditions, grantDesk/allocateServiceSlices, grantDesk/traceActivityClaims, grantDesk/composeEvidenceNarrative, grantDesk/assembleSubmissionVersion, grantDesk/classifyAmendmentEffectiveDate, grantDesk/allocateAcrossPeriods, grantDesk/reconcileSharedActivity, grantDesk/reviewParticipantDisclosure, grantDesk/amendSubmittedReport, grantDesk/grantMath/checkPeriodSliceTotals]
---
Bind saved = ledger.checkpoint when present, otherwise null. An absent checkpoint means this is the first review.

Bind amendmentWindow = `classifyAmendmentEffectiveDate(request, ledger.amendments)` before selecting any award terms. Bind conditions = `deriveAwardConditions(request, ledger.reports, ledger.policyCandidates, ledger.evidencePages, ledger.amendments, amendmentWindow)` and carry its affected expense IDs and unresolved effective dates as blockers into eligibility. A future-only change cannot authorize an earlier service period.

Before allocating, bind sharedActivity = `reconcileSharedActivity(request, ledger.sharedActivityLinks)` and periods = `allocateAcrossPeriods(request, ledger.periodAllocations)`. Bind periodCheck = `checkPeriodSliceTotals(periods.slices)` using exact integer minor units; the verifier rejects malformed values, mixed currency or scale, duplicate slice IDs, inconsistent original amounts, and any expense whose slices do not sum exactly to its original amount. Keep shared activity attribution distinct from expense allocation: each funded share must have its own documented basis, and service dates govern which reporting period receives a cost. Bind allocations = `allocateServiceSlices(request, conditions, periods, periodCheck, ledger.evidencePages, sharedActivity)`. Its typed result must withhold each expense lacking supported currency, period or allocation basis while retaining independently supported expenses; it is not an absent variable on a blocked branch.

Bind activities = `traceActivityClaims(request, conditions, allocations, ledger.evidencePages)`. Only accept a funded activity when it links to a valid condition and source evidence; return other claims in its unsupported or partial fields. Preserve partial delivery, unverified outcomes, and unproven impact as separate states. Bind disclosure = `reviewParticipantDisclosure(request, ledger.participantDisclosureRequests)` independently of activity verification; pass that exact `ParticipantDisclosureReview` to narrative composition. Identifiable data may enter only for allowedParticipantIds; withheld identifiers remain excluded. Prefer the review's allowed aggregate references where they answer the reporting requirement.

Bind narrative = `composeEvidenceNarrative(request, conditions, allocations, activities, ledger.evidencePages, disclosure)`; its narrative field is null with explicit blockedClaims when no period is reportable. Reconcile each claimed quantity against accepted allocations and activity evidence; keep deviations and missing impact evidence visible. Bind correctedVersion = `amendSubmittedReport(request, ledger.priorSubmissions)` when a prior submission exists, otherwise bind GrantCorrectionPlan { amendment: null, blockers: [], oldReceiptRefs: [] }. Preserve earlier receipts and supersede them only through a linked amendment. Bind submission = `assembleSubmissionVersion(request, narrative, ledger.evidencePages, correctedVersion)`. Its submission field stays null and dispatchReady false when the narrative, exact approval, deliverables or required linked correction remain blocked; preserve those precise questions in blockers. Bind guardrails as GrantGuardrail entries for actual amendment, period-conservation, shared-activity, disclosure and correction findings with their own evidence references and proposed follow-up actions. Bind checkpoint = reconcileGrantReportState(saved, request, ledger, conditions, allocations, activities, disclosure, correctedVersion, submission). Preserve the funder’s exact prior submission and receipt lineage. A correction amends a submitted report through a linked version and never erases its original receipt. Period conservation, shared activity attribution and participant disclosure decisions retain their source editions; changes reopen only the affected report periods. Return GrantProgramResult { caseId: request.caseId, conditions, allocations, activities, narrative, submission, guardrails, checkpoint, commitAllowed: false }. Local readiness never stands in for funder receipt. Host-controlled authorization and dispatch remain separate.
